message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Fiji macro for automated root-tip diameter measurement in Clarkia xantiana"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-04-24"
authors:
  - family-names: "D'Ascenzo"
    given-names: "Dominic"
    email: "dascenzod03@gmail.com"
    # Uncomment and fill in once you have an ORCID iD:
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # affiliation: "Your Institution / Department"
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/clarkia-root-tip-macro"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Fiji
  - ImageJ
  - macro
  - root morphology
  - root tip
  - Clarkia xantiana
  - image analysis
  - plant ecology
  - local adaptation
abstract: >-
  A Fiji/ImageJ macro that automatically measures radicle diameters at eight
  fixed distances from the root tip (0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 1.00, 1.25, 1.50, 1.75,
  and 2.00 mm) in calibrated grayscale images of Toluidine-Blue-stained
  Clarkia xantiana subsp. xantiana seedlings. Designed to support a study of
  geographic variation in root morphology across populations native to
  different soil types.
